  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Monday)\nIssued at 233 PM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nThursday into the weekend, temperatures near 100 on Thursday and \nFriday.  With the Four Corners high amplifying the flow will turn \nmore northwesterly, but given the position of the high further east, \nthe showers and storms look to come through the northeast Panhandle \non Thursday.  And by Friday the overall flow will turn more \nnortherly, which really lowers the precipitation chances. NBM is \ngiving about a 20 percent chance to the south, but overall the \nchances for showers and storms on Friday don't look great. As we \ncontinue into the weekend widespread 100 degrees expected with maybe \nsome heat products being needed.  Given the position of the high and \nthe overall flow being northerly to northeasterly, the chances of \nprecipitation are very low < 10 percent.  Monday could turn the \ncorner a bit as the potential to return to northwest flow is \npresent, including an increase thunderstorm potential for the \nnorthwest Panhandles 10-20 percent. \n\nWeber",
